  "summary": "Vibrant body painting tradition of the Surma people using natural pigments for ceremonial and social purposes.",
  "description": "Characterized by intricate white and red geometric patterns painted on the face and body using chalk and ochre pigments. The aesthetic developed as a form of social communication and ritual decoration, with specific designs denoting age, social status, and ceremonial occasions.",
